WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.643
CORE-V uses short labels for several different technical objects.

2
00:00:06.643 --> 00:00:11.242
CVE2 and CVA6 can name a family or code base.

3
00:00:11.242 --> 00:00:19.418
CV32E20, CV32E40X, and CV32A60AX identify more specific cores or configurations.

4
00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:32.601
This lesson builds a practical decoder across the embedded two-stage, embedded four-stage, and application-class six-stage lines.

5
00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:46.500
We will also connect the human-readable name to the repository, verified configuration, release, and the machine-readable identity CSRs.

